      "role": "user",
      "content": "i feel like a ghost lately. everything is so fast now, so loud and digital... i look around and i don't even recognize the world anymore. it feels like my part of the story is already written and the pages are just turning without me. like i'm just a relic waiting to be cleared away.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a very common feeling when the world feels too fast and loud, but you're not a relic; you are the one holding the pen right now. The pages turning without you is a metaphor for the world moving on, not a reflection of your worth. You are still the author of your story, even if you feel like you're just a character in someone else's plot.\n\nThe world is loud and digital, but that noise is just the background hum of a life that keeps going, and you can choose to listen to the quiet parts of it. Your story is not written; it is being written by your choices and your moments of stillness, which are right here in the present.\n\nYou are not disappearing; you are simply becoming one with the flow, and that flow is full of potential. The fact that you feel like a ghost is a sign that you have been stepping away from the action, but the story is waiting for you to return and rewrite the ending.",
